# Drupal contribution workspace (Claude Code)

Read `.drupal-contrib/context.md` in full before contribution work. It contains the shared site table, workflow, and issue-record rules.

Resolve `<skills-root>` to `.claude/skills`. Start with `/drupal-issue-start <url>`.
Delegate the named roles using the installed `.claude/agents/` definitions.
Preserve approved scope and relay agent pauses to the human.

The installer prepares `.claude/settings.json`, a Git guardrail hook, and
project-scoped MCP configuration in `.mcp.json`. Approve the project MCP server
in Claude Code when prompted; check it with `/mcp`.
Resolve any `.drupal-contrib/proposals/` notices before relying on that configuration.
Installed skills, agents, and hook scripts are overwritten on every re-run; before
customizing or deleting one, list its path under `localOverrides` in
`.drupal-contrib/install.json` so the change survives.

Every drafted issue, MR description, and comment ends with an AI disclosure (or fills the template's AI disclosure section, if it has one) — collapsible on GitLab as below, one italic line on classic Drupal.org — never a tool or model name; `<uses>` is any of `research`, `writing`, `code`, in that order (full rules: `drupalorg-comment-format`):
```
<details><summary>AI disclosure</summary>

_Used AI to help with <uses> (<what it did>). The reasoning and positions are my own, and I reviewed everything before posting. ([Drupal.org AI policy](https://www.drupal.org/docs/develop/issues/issue-procedures-and-etiquette/policy-on-the-use-of-ai-when-contributing-to-drupal#s-disclosure))_

</details>
```
